"""
Keyframe Tools Interval - v3.2.1 (Blender 5.2.4 LTS)

Delete or bake keyframes at an interval on:
  * Selected bones   (Pose Mode): location / rotation / scale + numeric bone custom properties
  * Selected objects (Object Mode): location / rotation / scale

Install:
  Edit > Preferences > Add-ons > Install from Disk
  Select this .py file, enable the add-on, then open the 3D Viewport Sidebar (N).

Panel:
  3D Viewport > Sidebar (N) > Item tab > Keyframe Interval Tools

Blender 5.2.4 compatibility:
  * Uses Blender's slotted Action / Action Slot / Channelbag animation API.
  * Does not use the removed Action.fcurves API on Blender 5.x.
  * Resolves PoseBone selection before legacy Bone selection fallbacks.
  * Uses the assigned Action slot when finding or creating F-Curves.
  * Baking updates keys already on a sampled frame instead of creating duplicates.

Interval behaviour is unchanged:
  * End Frame is exclusive.
  * Interval 0: process every frame in the frame range.
  * Interval N: keep Start, Start + (N + 1), ...
      - Normal: process all frames between those kept frames.
      - Inverse: process only the kept frames.
"""

